Subject: [PATCH] media: name the communications device on every host

A Windows persona lists Windows' virtual communications audio device
(0131). Chromium only knows its name on Windows builds and hits
NOTREACHED elsewhere, which crashed the browser on enumerateDevices() on
a Linux host without a sound card. Other builds now return the English
Windows name.

diff --git a/media/audio/audio_device_description.cc b/media/audio/audio_device_description.cc
index d9d394b..1846523 100644
--- a/media/audio/audio_device_description.cc
+++ b/media/audio/audio_device_description.cc
@@ -157,7 +157,9 @@ std::string AudioDeviceDescription::GetCommunicationsDeviceName() {
   // is deprecated.
   return "";
 #else
-  NOTREACHED();
+  // A Windows persona lists Windows' virtual communications device on any
+  // host; this is the name Windows gives it in English.
+  return "Communications";
 #endif
 }
 
